^SAMPLE = GSM4818509
!Sample_title = Healthy-s110-1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4818509
!Sample_status = Public on Oct 06 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 05 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Oct 06 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = 3D engineered tissue, myobundle
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: engineered skeletal muscle
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = culture age: 2 weeks of 3D differentiation culture
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: wildtype
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: none
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary muscle cells were isolated from biopsies using the outgrowth method, expanded for 5 passages in T175 flasks, and used to construct 3D myobundles. 3D myobundles were cultured for 4 days in 3D growth media followed by 2 weeks of 3D differentiation.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNeasy Fibrous Tissue Mini Kit (Qiagen)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA libraries were prepared for sequencing using standard Illumina protocols
!Sample_description = Pompe_vs_healthy-expression_matrix.csv
!Sample_description = healthy-s110
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina NovaSeq 6000 reads were processed using the TrimGalore toolkit v0.4.1 to trim low quality bases and Illumina sequencing adapters from the 3’ end of the reads.  Only reads that were 20nt or longer after trimming were kept for further analysis. Read quality was checked for each sample using FastQC v0.11.2.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were mapped to the GRCh38v93 version of the human genome and transcriptome using the STAR RNA-seq alignment tool v2.5.0c.  Reads were kept for subsequent analysis if they mapped to a single genomic location.
!Sample_data_processing = Gene counts were compiled using the HTSeq tool v0.6.1.  Only genes that had at least 10 reads in any given library were used in subsequent analysis.
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization and differential expression was carried out using the DESeq2 Bioconductor package v1.16.1 with the R statistical programming environment v3.4.1_3.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38v93
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: normalized expression matrix in csv format
